      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Following a prolonged and unsuccessful treatment, 50 patients with severe compression-radical forms of lumbar osteochondritis received--under roentgenographic control--a course of epidural injections of drugs (trimecaine, chymotrypsin and lydasa). A considerable improvement was observed in 60% of the patients, which indicates that the method is effective."},
